WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.468
[music playing]

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:04.003
That was a
wonderful performance.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.004
I wish I could stay.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.206
I think I sang really well.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.341
You always sing well.

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:10.844
But we haven't found
it yet, have we?

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.178
Not for lack of trying.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:14.180
So let's get you
back into the studio,

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.448
and put our heads together.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.082
Hammond.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:16.983
Ted.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.785
Listen, I, uh, I
wish I could linger,

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:19.819
but I have another event.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:20.653
Congratulations.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:21.755
Glad you could make it.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:29.129
On your birthday, last year,
you remember what you wish for?

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.864
Have you seen my father?

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.966
You said you wanted to
be on the Steve Allen show.

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:34.667
And what did I say to you?

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.170
I said, I was going to
make your dreams come true.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:38.405
And now look at where we are.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.306
He made it all this
way, stayed for the show,

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:41.474
and didn't stay for
the party, which

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.243
means he was either
still mad at me,

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.844
or, he thought my
performance was bad.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:45.678
Was it?

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:48.815
No, baby, baby,
baby, no, come on.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:49.716
Mr. Wexler?

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:53.887
I'm a big fan Aretha.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.021
Ms. Franklin.

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:57.724
Excuse me, Miss Franklin.

00:00:57.791 --> 00:01:00.360
You know, I've
launched a few careers.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:03.129
Atlantic records and me,
we roll up our sleeves,

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:04.130
and we dig deep.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:06.366
This contract with
Columbia is almost up.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:09.135
What she does after
that, that's her call.

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.703
Columbia's had a good run.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.005
But music's changing.

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:15.809
You got to stay ahead of it, or
you're gonna get left behind.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:16.976
Can I be honest?

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:18.411
Yeah, please.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:21.848
Tonight, I wanted to be wowed.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:22.816
But I wasn't.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.083
I don't think the
audience was, either.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.351
Well, now you're
just plain wrong.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:26.986
"Skylark" is going
to be classic.

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.488
I'm trying everything I can.

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:30.089
You know I work
with Ray Charles?

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.224
Genius.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:34.461
I could do for you,
what I did for Ray.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:37.197
I could help you
find your sound.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.065
That's what I do.

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:41.568
Now, let me ask you,
what kind of music

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:44.904
do you really want to
make, Miss Franklin?

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:48.174
I want to make
hits, Mr. Wexler.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:51.711
You'll get there, when
you realize you are Aretha

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:55.748
Franklin, and nobody else.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:56.649
Pleasure.

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:01.855
Let me freshen your drink.

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:06.826
[music playing]

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:39.559
(SINGING) How I got over.

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:42.328
How I got over.

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:47.901
You know my soul looks back
and wonder how I got over.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:50.870
How I got over.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:53.673
How I got over.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:59.012
You know my soul looks
back and wonder how I over.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:05.118
Just as soon as I see Jesus,
the man who made me free.

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:07.487
You know, the man, who
bleed and suffered.

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:10.490
You know, he died
for you and me.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:13.626
I wanna thank you,
because you brought me.

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:16.296
I wanna thank you, Jesus,
because you taught me.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:19.132
I wanna thank you
because you kept me.

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:21.634
I wanna thank you,
cause you never left me.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.970
I wanna sing.

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:27.674
Oh, [inaudible].

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:33.212
My soul looks back and
wonder how I got over.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:35.949
How I got over.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:38.518
How I got over.

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:44.290
You know, my soul looks back
and wonder how I got over.

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:49.829
How I got over, How I got over.

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:55.134
You know, my soul looks back
and wonder how I got over.

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.202
[applause]

